      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T14:11:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Tried this both alone and combined with the row unroll below, measured on real Neoverse N1. Alone (16-wide columns, no row unroll) it was slower than the existing 8-wide loop at every size tested. Combined with the row unroll -- two independent 8-column groups carried through the same unrolled core so their load/shift latency can overlap -- it\u0027s faster than either unroll alone from 64x32 up, up to +22% at 256x256 (the largest restoration unit size). Kept the combined version, with an 8-wide leftover pass for a [8,16) remainder and the existing C fallback below that.",
      "revId": "aedd5846eff3ce817d80464706151582a576d459",
